  "raw": "\n\nMonday marks the first time since 2011 that the Southern California region receives an extended period of rain and snow.\n\nSierra snowpacks, called California's stored water, are also unusually high and significantly improved during the wet season that started Oct. 1, or between 30% and 60% of normal.\n\nThe Natural Resources Agency delays any restoration of the Californian Orwo program, under which an agency collects waste water from thousands of Cupertino, Frisco and Mountain View homeowners using underground pipes.\n\nPeople who can show a postseason profit (over $21k), be a new business, or a single issued company are all welcome to apply for the Room in the Inn membership. Guests will get an extra 15% off at any In N' On location, making it an even more appealing option when compared with other lodging options. You can also enjoy free wifi, daily card fastener rooms open to the sky, free breakfast buffets, summer night outdoor pool and on",
  "serialized": "Monday marks the first time since 2011 that the Southern California region receives an extended period of rain and snow. Sierra snowpacks, called California's stored water, are also unusually high and significantly improved during the wet season that started Oct. 1, or between 30% and 60% of normal. The Natural Resources Agency delays any restoration of the Californian Orwo program, under which an agency collects waste water from thousands of Cupertino, Frisco and Mountain View homeowners using underground pipes. People who can show a postseason profit (over $21k), be a new business, or a single issued company are all welcome to apply for the Room in the Inn membership. Guests will get an extra 15% off at any In N' On location, making it an even more appealing option when compared with other lodging options. You can also enjoy free wifi, daily card fastener rooms open to the sky, free breakfast buffets, summer night outdoor pool and on",
